# holds the objective lane. Written fresh against the U1-conform claims file.
# Journal: u1-conform-audit-analyst.jsonl.
cd "C:/Users/mikes/WebstormProjects/scaffold" || exit 9
timeout 3600 codex exec --json -C "C:/Users/mikes/WebstormProjects/scaffold" --sandbox read-only --model gpt-6-astra -c 'model_reasoning_effort="high"' --output-last-message "units/u1-conform-audit-analyst-last.md" "You hold the OBJECTIVE lane (correctness, constraints, what the code, the rules, and the installed declarations permit) of the audit of the U1-conform unit, which native Opus wrote in the Veneer checkout at C:/Users/mikes/WebstormProjects/veneer. The claims file ./tmp/audit/u1-conform-audit-claims.md alone fixes the claim numbers: rule on every claim it carries, and only those, with CONFIRMED, REFUTED, or UNDECIDABLE and the deciding evidence (file:line or exact text). The Orchestrator rendered the diff over d8b0e65 including every untracked file at ./tmp/audit/u1-conform-diff.patch and the status at ./tmp/audit/u1-conform-status.txt; read those, the live Veneer files, the retained records under ./.orkestrel/veneer/ (veneer-conformance-verdict.md and units/veneer-conformance-reviewer-report.md for the findings the unit closes, units/u1-conform-brief.md, units/u1-conform-report.md), and the law under this checkout (AGENTS.md and .claude/rules/). Check each of the writer's recorded decisions against the rule it cites, read every moved class and renamed helper for behaviour that changed with the move, and read the distribution proof's new built-artifact case for what it proves against the installed tarball. Run no command that writes. Add extra findings no claim names, numbered after the last claim, with sites. End with one terminal line: Verdict: accept, or Verdict: fix round with the claims that force it." < /dev/null > "units/u1-conform-audit-analyst.jsonl" 2> "units/u1-conform-audit-analyst.err"
echo "exit=$?" >> "units/u1-conform-audit-analyst.err"
